1
00:00:09,250 --> 00:00:10,650
(Lee Min Jung)

2
00:00:14,090 --> 00:00:15,450
(Kim Ji Seok)

3
00:00:21,990 --> 00:00:24,930
(OK! Let's Get Divorced)

4
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:26,430
(All child actor scenes were filmed with a guardian present...)

5
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:27,930
(with professional staff and in accordance with safety guidelines.)

6
00:00:33,070 --> 00:00:37,010
I finally realized what is truly important.

7
00:00:38,980 --> 00:00:41,010
And what is truly precious.

8
00:00:43,110 --> 00:00:44,120
What is it?

9
00:00:46,950 --> 00:00:51,060
Not obsessing over what I cannot have for too long.

10
00:00:53,690 --> 00:00:56,800
Not missing out on the happiness right in front of me.

11
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:03,230
After you...

12
00:01:03,300 --> 00:01:05,540
completely disappeared from my sight,

13
00:01:05,540 --> 00:01:06,540
I realized it.

14
00:01:11,940 --> 00:01:13,880
So please don't leave anymore.

15
00:01:16,750 --> 00:01:18,050
Just stay by my side.

16
00:01:22,990 --> 00:01:24,190
You will do that, right?

17
00:01:27,960 --> 00:01:28,960
Right?

18
00:02:03,330 --> 00:02:04,400
(Final Episode)

19
00:02:04,460 --> 00:02:05,530
Won Ho.

20
00:02:08,300 --> 00:02:09,470
Won Ho.

21
00:02:24,520 --> 00:02:26,280
(To Mi Young.)

22
00:02:30,760 --> 00:02:31,760
To Mi Young.

23
00:02:33,060 --> 00:02:34,160
Mi Young,

24
00:02:34,830 --> 00:02:37,100
I do not know how long it has been since I called your name...

25
00:02:37,100 --> 00:02:38,730
through a letter like this.

26
00:02:41,130 --> 00:02:44,200
This will probably be the last letter I write to you.

27
00:02:47,840 --> 00:02:48,940
I am sorry, Mi Young.

28
00:02:50,140 --> 00:02:54,550
I wanted to make you the happiest woman in the world.

29
00:02:54,580 --> 00:02:56,680
But I could not. I am sorry.

30
00:02:58,080 --> 00:02:59,620
I am sorry for making you lonely.

31
00:03:00,850 --> 00:03:02,620
I am sorry for hurting you.

32
00:03:06,560 --> 00:03:09,630
When you said Dallae went wrong because of the medicine...

33
00:03:09,690 --> 00:03:13,460
Will that bring our dead Dallae back to life?

34
00:03:13,530 --> 00:03:16,830
- Get out. I said get out. - Do not worry, I am leaving.

35
00:03:21,610 --> 00:03:24,280
I should have listened to you more closely back then.

36
00:03:27,380 --> 00:03:31,050
It turns out Kyung Tae tampered with the medicine on purpose.

37
00:03:33,990 --> 00:03:35,150
Kyung Tae told me.

38
00:03:36,960 --> 00:03:39,190
He was afraid I would leave him.

39
00:03:41,190 --> 00:03:42,690
That is why he did such a terrible thing...

40
00:03:44,300 --> 00:03:46,400
to our Dallae and to you.

41
00:03:48,200 --> 00:03:50,570
I thought I knew Kyung Tae well all this time.

42
00:03:50,640 --> 00:03:53,200
Why did you do that to Mi Young? Tell me.

43
00:03:53,270 --> 00:03:56,340
- I'm such an idiot. - I cannot even blame Kyung Tae.

44
00:03:58,340 --> 00:03:59,340
Everything...

45
00:04:00,380 --> 00:04:02,210
Everything is all my fault.

46
00:04:05,620 --> 00:04:07,450
Even though we are ending like this,

47
00:04:09,390 --> 00:04:13,760
I want to make sure the rest of your life is a happy ending.

48
00:04:18,960 --> 00:04:20,060
Lastly, Mi Young.

49
00:04:22,130 --> 00:04:24,800
- Won Ho! - Thank you for everything.

50
00:04:26,040 --> 00:04:28,310
I love you, Mi Young.

51
00:04:57,800 --> 00:04:58,970
Won Ho!

52
00:05:01,710 --> 00:05:02,710
Won Ho.

53
00:05:04,110 --> 00:05:05,340
Wait!

54
00:05:07,380 --> 00:05:08,410
Won Ho.

55
00:05:10,920 --> 00:05:13,690
Won Ho, wait.

56
00:05:20,690 --> 00:05:22,260
Won Ho!

57
00:05:22,330 --> 00:05:25,830
Won Ho, wait. Just wait a second. Don't go.

58
00:05:25,900 --> 00:05:27,730
Won Ho, don't go.

59
00:05:35,470 --> 00:05:39,380
Won Ho, I cannot go any further.

60
00:05:40,780 --> 00:05:42,310
Right, don't come, Mi Young.

61
00:05:43,680 --> 00:05:45,580
Do not...

62
00:05:45,580 --> 00:05:47,090
follow me anymore.

63
00:05:48,490 --> 00:05:49,850
Won Ho.

64
00:05:51,690 --> 00:05:53,560
You saw what I wrote in the letter, right?

65
00:05:56,690 --> 00:05:57,700
I am sorry!

66
00:05:58,900 --> 00:05:59,930
I am really...

67
00:06:01,900 --> 00:06:04,170
I am so truly sorry, Mi Young.

68
00:06:04,240 --> 00:06:07,310
No, that's...

69
00:06:07,370 --> 00:06:09,840
That's not your fault, Won Ho.

70
00:06:10,210 --> 00:06:12,840
No. It is all my fault.

71
00:06:13,850 --> 00:06:15,550
I will be guilty toward you...

72
00:06:17,180 --> 00:06:18,620
for the rest of my life.

73
00:06:21,890 --> 00:06:22,950
Mi Young, I think...

74
00:06:25,820 --> 00:06:27,660
it is really time now.

75
00:06:28,660 --> 00:06:29,730
Won Ho...

76
00:06:31,360 --> 00:06:32,360
Let's...

77
00:06:34,600 --> 00:06:36,300
Let's get a divorce!

78
00:06:39,840 --> 00:06:43,340
You will understand how I feel, right?

79
00:06:43,740 --> 00:06:45,040
No!

80
00:06:45,640 --> 00:06:47,850
No, I don't understand!

81
00:06:53,280 --> 00:06:54,320
But...

82
00:06:56,590 --> 00:06:58,160
if that's what you want...

83
00:07:00,830 --> 00:07:01,830
Fine.

84
00:07:03,430 --> 00:07:04,460
Let's get divorced.

85
00:07:08,870 --> 00:07:09,870
Okay.

86
00:07:11,440 --> 00:07:13,000
Let's...

87
00:07:13,070 --> 00:07:14,870
Fine, let's get divorced!

88
00:07:22,950 --> 00:07:27,050
What was the meaning of the tears we shed back then?

89
00:07:28,720 --> 00:07:32,590
Was it regret for the days we misunderstood and hurt each other?

90
00:07:33,860 --> 00:07:35,590
Were we holding on to things...

91
00:07:37,530 --> 00:07:38,800
that were already gone?

92
00:07:41,330 --> 00:07:44,100
- Do you even know? - Gosh, Mi Young.

93
00:07:44,170 --> 00:07:48,470
Don't wear pants like that. You have a hole in your knee, jerk!

94
00:07:48,540 --> 00:07:51,880
Then what am I supposed to do? I'm so furious that you tricked me,

95
00:07:51,940 --> 00:07:53,780
I can't do the broadcast or anything else.

96
00:07:53,850 --> 00:07:55,950
What am I supposed to do?

97
00:07:56,010 --> 00:07:59,450
If only we had been a little kinder to each other...

98
00:08:04,660 --> 00:08:05,660
I...

99
00:08:06,990 --> 00:08:08,730
took the medicine my husband gave me...

100
00:08:10,160 --> 00:08:11,560
and lost my baby.

101
00:08:11,700 --> 00:08:13,130
If only we had been...

102
00:08:14,200 --> 00:08:16,100
a little more honest with each other...

103
00:08:18,240 --> 00:08:19,970
If either of us...

104
00:08:20,040 --> 00:08:23,640
had the courage to take the first step toward the other...

105
00:08:25,410 --> 00:08:28,080
Would our reality be different now?

106
00:08:41,090 --> 00:08:43,030
There's no way to know.

107
00:08:43,130 --> 00:08:46,130
What is certain is that we can never...

108
00:08:47,670 --> 00:08:49,930
go back to the past.

109
00:08:50,940 --> 00:08:52,300
(Yeonnam Family Court)

110
00:08:54,770 --> 00:08:57,880
And today, we are...

111
00:09:00,480 --> 00:09:01,550
getting a divorce.

112
00:09:10,760 --> 00:09:12,490
Mi Young.

113
00:09:12,560 --> 00:09:15,430
Did you talk about anything else with your husband?

114
00:09:16,830 --> 00:09:17,830
No.

115
00:09:21,200 --> 00:09:23,730
Then why does he look so serious?

116
00:09:23,800 --> 00:09:24,800
It's making me nervous.

117
00:09:28,040 --> 00:09:31,240
Anyway, let's not let our guard down until the very end.

118
00:09:34,850 --> 00:09:36,150
Mi Young?

119
00:09:36,210 --> 00:09:38,950
Yes? Oh, right.

120
00:09:39,020 --> 00:09:42,390
Have you made up your mind?

121
00:09:42,490 --> 00:09:45,090
- What? - I said hurry up and decide.

122
00:09:45,620 --> 00:09:47,290
What we're going to eat after the trial.

123
00:09:47,360 --> 00:09:50,330
We need to decide these things in advance to save time.

124
00:09:50,390 --> 00:09:53,530
- You can decide that yourself. - Oh, come on.

125
00:09:54,670 --> 00:09:55,670
All right, then.

126
00:10:01,570 --> 00:10:03,810
(Jihwaja Motel)

127
00:10:08,910 --> 00:10:09,910
Mom.

128
00:10:09,980 --> 00:10:12,520
Did you see the new spicy webfoot octopus place next to the market?

129
00:10:12,580 --> 00:10:14,390
I hope they don't go out of business and last a long time this time.

130
00:10:16,620 --> 00:10:17,990
Mom!

131
00:10:18,360 --> 00:10:20,960
- Yes. - What are you thinking about?

132
00:10:22,060 --> 00:10:24,700
Won Ho went to court today.

133
00:10:24,760 --> 00:10:26,130
Oh, right.

134
00:10:26,430 --> 00:10:28,230
Oh, that's today.

135
00:10:28,300 --> 00:10:30,200
Did Won Ho call?

136
00:10:30,270 --> 00:10:31,640
No.

137
00:10:31,940 --> 00:10:35,110
Don't worry too much, Mom. Won Ho and my sister-in-law...

138
00:10:36,370 --> 00:10:38,880
Oh, I guess I shouldn't call her my sister-in-law anymore.

139
00:10:38,940 --> 00:10:41,410
Anyway, what worse could happen now?

140
00:10:41,510 --> 00:10:43,510
Do you remember?

141
00:10:43,580 --> 00:10:45,780
When you and your ex split up,

142
00:10:45,850 --> 00:10:48,120
you told me not to worry.

143
00:10:48,190 --> 00:10:51,120
And then you let your ex take Ha Neul away completely...

144
00:10:51,190 --> 00:10:53,190
and came back empty-handed.

145
00:10:53,260 --> 00:10:55,330
Did I do that?

146
00:10:55,390 --> 00:10:58,230
But I got Ha Neul back anyway. So it's fine.

147
00:10:58,330 --> 00:10:59,960
You call that getting him back?

148
00:11:00,030 --> 00:11:03,670
Ha Neul's mom was just too busy, so she had to give him back.

149
00:11:03,730 --> 00:11:04,740
Right.

150
00:11:06,300 --> 00:11:08,370
Do you always have to say it like that?

151
00:11:08,440 --> 00:11:09,870
Is Ha Neul some kind of object?

152
00:11:09,940 --> 00:11:14,580
I had a bad dream last night, and I am feeling really anxious.

153
00:11:15,250 --> 00:11:18,180
I feel like Won Ho is going to cause some kind of trouble.

154
00:11:24,360 --> 00:11:25,720
We cannot agree to that.

155
00:11:29,490 --> 00:11:33,200
The plaintiff is demanding a property division amount...

156
00:11:33,260 --> 00:11:35,900
on the condition of giving up the management of the company,

157
00:11:37,400 --> 00:11:38,840
but we cannot accept it.

158
00:11:38,900 --> 00:11:43,070
The plaintiff's requested amount is 790,000 dollars in total.

159
00:11:43,140 --> 00:11:47,280
We cannot accept this amount.

160
00:11:48,050 --> 00:11:49,750
What do you mean you cannot accept it?

161
00:11:50,380 --> 00:11:53,720
Did you properly review the contents of the complaint we sent?

162
00:11:53,780 --> 00:11:56,990
Of course. I read it over and over,

163
00:11:57,050 --> 00:11:59,020
and I read it again this morning.

164
00:11:59,090 --> 00:12:00,620
Then you must be well aware...

165
00:12:00,620 --> 00:12:03,060
that the plaintiff acted as the actual owner,

166
00:12:03,130 --> 00:12:04,530
must you not?

167
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:07,000
I see.

168
00:12:10,700 --> 00:12:12,070
Mediator.

169
00:12:12,140 --> 00:12:15,010
Throughout their marriage, the plaintiff...

170
00:12:15,070 --> 00:12:18,140
supported the defendant with absolute devotion.

171
00:12:18,710 --> 00:12:20,140
By serving as co-CEO...

172
00:12:20,210 --> 00:12:22,080
of the company under the defendant's name,

173
00:12:22,150 --> 00:12:24,420
she turned an unknown startup...

174
00:12:24,480 --> 00:12:27,790
into an influential wedding shop in just three years...

175
00:12:27,850 --> 00:12:30,050
This was all possible because of the plaintiff's...

176
00:12:30,120 --> 00:12:32,360
blood, sweat, and tears.

177
00:12:32,420 --> 00:12:35,690
On the other hand, the defendant left everything...

178
00:12:35,760 --> 00:12:40,100
other than making dresses entirely up to the plaintiff.

179
00:12:41,400 --> 00:12:43,500
The company grew this much...

180
00:12:43,570 --> 00:12:48,110
- all to the plaintiff's efforts? - That is correct!

181
00:12:48,170 --> 00:12:50,110
If the plaintiff and the defendant divorce,

182
00:12:50,170 --> 00:12:53,210
the plaintiff will naturally have to leave the company,

183
00:12:53,280 --> 00:12:54,710
so she is asking for her contributions to the company...

184
00:12:54,780 --> 00:12:58,520
to be recognized in the property division.

185
00:12:58,580 --> 00:12:59,880
What exactly is the problem?

186
00:12:59,950 --> 00:13:03,450
- This is completely absurd. - How dare she...

187
00:13:03,520 --> 00:13:04,660
I think...

188
00:13:04,720 --> 00:13:06,820
you just spoke informally.

189
00:13:07,830 --> 00:13:11,030
- You heard that, right, Mediator? - Please calm down.

190
00:13:11,100 --> 00:13:13,130
Yes, well... Why you...

191
00:13:14,500 --> 00:13:15,500
Defendant,

192
00:13:15,570 --> 00:13:18,970
- do you deny the claims? - No.

193
00:13:19,470 --> 00:13:20,540
I acknowledge them.

194
00:13:21,570 --> 00:13:23,740
The plaintiff's contributions to the company...

195
00:13:23,810 --> 00:13:27,550
must be acknowledged. No, it is actually more than that.

196
00:13:28,610 --> 00:13:31,650
In fact, without the plaintiff, this company...

197
00:13:31,720 --> 00:13:34,620
would have gone bankrupt a long time ago.

198
00:13:35,290 --> 00:13:36,650
What?

199
00:13:36,720 --> 00:13:39,390
Defendant, what exactly are you trying to say?

200
00:13:40,620 --> 00:13:41,860
Yes.

201
00:13:41,930 --> 00:13:45,460
Then I will clarify everything right now.

202
00:13:45,830 --> 00:13:47,500
We...

203
00:13:47,570 --> 00:13:49,300
highly acknowledge the plaintiff's devotion...

204
00:13:49,370 --> 00:13:52,140
to the defendant and the company during their marriage,

205
00:13:52,200 --> 00:13:54,640
and therefore,

206
00:13:55,770 --> 00:13:58,880
we believe the property division of 790,000 dollars...

207
00:13:58,940 --> 00:14:01,580
is actually too small.

208
00:14:02,050 --> 00:14:03,910
Therefore, on the condition that the plaintiff...

209
00:14:03,980 --> 00:14:06,550
takes over the management of the company...

210
00:14:06,620 --> 00:14:10,220
instead of giving it up,

211
00:14:10,290 --> 00:14:12,920
we will accept the property division of 790,000 dollars...

212
00:14:12,990 --> 00:14:14,190
to be given to her.

213
00:14:22,730 --> 00:14:24,030
Here.

214
00:14:24,670 --> 00:14:25,770
Won Ho.

215
00:14:28,040 --> 00:14:29,370
What is wrong with him?

216
00:14:29,440 --> 00:14:31,180
Did he take out a loan with company money?

217
00:14:33,310 --> 00:14:36,250
No, the corporate registry is clean.

218
00:14:36,310 --> 00:14:37,650
Plaintiff.

219
00:14:37,750 --> 00:14:39,750
In the claims the plaintiff made against the defendant,

220
00:14:39,820 --> 00:14:42,190
the management rights were not specified,

221
00:14:42,990 --> 00:14:45,760
but if you accept the defendant's proposal here right now,

222
00:14:45,820 --> 00:14:47,590
a voluntary mediation is possible.

223
00:14:47,660 --> 00:14:49,630
Will you accept the defendant's proposal?

224
00:14:51,300 --> 00:14:53,360
Mi Young, just accept it for now.

225
00:14:55,170 --> 00:14:57,000
Is it not a good thing to get the management rights?

226
00:15:11,250 --> 00:15:12,250
No.

227
00:15:13,850 --> 00:15:15,520
I cannot accept the management rights.

228
00:15:19,590 --> 00:15:21,030
Are you serious, Mi Young?

229
00:15:22,290 --> 00:15:23,530
Yes, Lawyer Jeon.

230
00:15:24,190 --> 00:15:25,830
It is the management rights, of all things.

231
00:15:28,030 --> 00:15:29,270
My client says...

232
00:15:29,900 --> 00:15:31,700
she will not accept the management rights.

233
00:15:33,300 --> 00:15:36,640
Please only negotiate regarding the property division.

234
00:15:36,710 --> 00:15:39,580
- Defendant, did you hear that? - Yes.

235
00:15:40,080 --> 00:15:43,710
As the plaintiff's counsel mentioned earlier,

236
00:15:43,780 --> 00:15:47,320
the plaintiff is the actual owner of the company...

237
00:15:47,380 --> 00:15:50,620
and is responsible for most of the management duties.

238
00:15:50,690 --> 00:15:51,860
That's not all.

239
00:15:52,460 --> 00:15:53,590
Not only with household chores,

240
00:15:53,660 --> 00:15:57,560
but also taking care of all the in-laws' affairs,

241
00:15:57,630 --> 00:15:59,930
the plaintiff, as a spouse, has truly...

242
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:03,270
played a near-perfect role.

243
00:16:05,040 --> 00:16:07,170
Therefore, our defendant...

244
00:16:07,240 --> 00:16:09,610
wishes to generously repay...

245
00:16:09,670 --> 00:16:13,480
the plaintiff for her past dedication...

246
00:16:13,540 --> 00:16:16,110
and believes that she should naturally take...

247
00:16:16,180 --> 00:16:19,350
not only the property division...

248
00:16:19,420 --> 00:16:22,990
but also the company's management rights.

249
00:16:29,060 --> 00:16:30,230
I said she is not accepting them.

250
00:16:30,290 --> 00:16:32,630
Stop refusing and just take them when offered.

251
00:16:32,700 --> 00:16:35,070
Opportunities like this are not common.

252
00:16:41,110 --> 00:16:42,770
As I have said,

253
00:16:43,410 --> 00:16:44,810
our plaintiff...

254
00:16:44,880 --> 00:16:48,950
- will not accept management rights. - Then...

255
00:16:49,550 --> 00:16:51,420
are you going to give up the property division too?

256
00:16:51,480 --> 00:16:54,020
Are you saying that if we do not accept the management rights,

257
00:16:54,080 --> 00:16:56,250
you will not agree to the property division either?

258
00:16:56,320 --> 00:16:58,260
Did I not mention that at the beginning?

259
00:16:58,320 --> 00:16:59,760
If you give up the management rights,

260
00:16:59,820 --> 00:17:02,230
we cannot accept the property division.

261
00:17:02,290 --> 00:17:04,060
I knew it.

262
00:17:04,130 --> 00:17:05,760
Tell me honestly.

263
00:17:05,830 --> 00:17:07,300
The management rights are just an excuse,

264
00:17:07,360 --> 00:17:08,470
and you have no intention of negotiating...

265
00:17:08,530 --> 00:17:10,000
the property division, do you?

266
00:17:10,070 --> 00:17:13,240
Is there perhaps a problem with the defendant's finances?

267
00:17:13,300 --> 00:17:14,640
Not at all.

268
00:17:14,710 --> 00:17:17,670
Our defendant's financial status is very solid.

269
00:17:19,680 --> 00:17:21,480
Can you prove that?

270
00:17:22,050 --> 00:17:23,510
That is difficult right now.

271
00:17:23,580 --> 00:17:25,220
- What? - I came here...

272
00:17:26,250 --> 00:17:28,720
- empty-handed today. - I have had enough of this!

273
00:17:28,790 --> 00:17:31,420
- I am really empty-handed. - Are you kidding me right now?

274
00:17:31,490 --> 00:17:33,290
Does it sound like I am kidding?

275
00:17:33,360 --> 00:17:34,590
Please be quiet, Plaintiff and Defendant.

276
00:17:34,660 --> 00:17:36,690
Defendant, do not provoke the plaintiff.

277
00:17:36,760 --> 00:17:38,500
Plaintiff's counsel, please sit down.

278
00:17:38,560 --> 00:17:40,000
Do not just stand there like that.

279
00:17:41,060 --> 00:17:44,000
- Please be quiet, Counselor. - Lawyer Bae.

280
00:17:44,070 --> 00:17:45,070
Mi Young!

281
00:17:51,680 --> 00:17:53,140
(Yeonnam Family Court Notice Board)

282
00:17:53,210 --> 00:17:56,510
- How can you just leave like this? - What about you, Won Ho?

283
00:17:56,580 --> 00:17:58,550
What is this, all of a sudden?

284
00:17:58,620 --> 00:18:00,480
Why are you handing the management rights over to me?

285
00:18:00,550 --> 00:18:02,450
I kept thinking about it until today also.

286
00:18:03,990 --> 00:18:05,060
Wait a minute.

287
00:18:05,490 --> 00:18:06,990
But is this really something to get so angry about...

288
00:18:07,060 --> 00:18:08,730
that you would storm out like this?

289
00:18:08,960 --> 00:18:10,830
You are getting the property division you wanted,

290
00:18:10,890 --> 00:18:12,600
and you get the management rights on top of that.

291
00:18:12,660 --> 00:18:13,700
What is so bad about that?

292
00:18:16,030 --> 00:18:18,670
Yes, I am sorry for bringing it up so suddenly.

293
00:18:18,740 --> 00:18:19,740
But...

294
00:18:20,940 --> 00:18:24,310
think about it carefully. The management rights are for you.

295
00:18:24,370 --> 00:18:27,680
- You did all this just for me? - Of course.

296
00:18:27,740 --> 00:18:29,410
I did it all for you, obviously.

297
00:18:31,680 --> 00:18:34,590
You have done nothing but suffer for the seven years we were married.

298
00:18:34,650 --> 00:18:36,690
You have been through so much all this time,

299
00:18:36,750 --> 00:18:38,060
so how would a few dollars from the divorce settlement...

300
00:18:38,120 --> 00:18:39,560
be any consolation?

301
00:18:40,620 --> 00:18:42,190
You should at least have the company...

302
00:18:42,260 --> 00:18:45,900
- so you feel less wronged. - Then what is left for you?

303
00:18:46,330 --> 00:18:47,660
If you hand over the company, the only thing you'll get...

304
00:18:47,730 --> 00:18:51,100
after the divorce, what do you plan to do then?

305
00:18:51,170 --> 00:18:53,400
I am a designer, Mi Young.

306
00:18:54,040 --> 00:18:57,310
As long as I have my skills, I can make dresses anywhere.

307
00:18:57,610 --> 00:19:01,780
There is absolutely no reason why my place has to be at J&White.

308
00:19:03,750 --> 00:19:05,720
Even so, this is a bit...

309
00:19:05,780 --> 00:19:06,780
Mi Young.

310
00:19:08,250 --> 00:19:10,190
- Let us go for now. - What?

311
00:19:12,220 --> 00:19:13,960
Let us go grab something to eat too.

312
00:19:16,230 --> 00:19:19,400
- Let us go that way. - Gosh...

313
00:19:21,730 --> 00:19:23,730
They do not call him snake for nothing.

314
00:19:25,570 --> 00:19:26,570
What?

315
00:19:27,800 --> 00:19:29,010
If you do not accept the management rights,

316
00:19:29,070 --> 00:19:31,170
he will not agree to the property division?

317
00:19:31,240 --> 00:19:33,810
Who is he trying to fool? What a scam.

318
00:19:36,410 --> 00:19:37,710
Mi Young,

319
00:19:37,780 --> 00:19:39,820
I will make sure you get your share of the property no matter what,

320
00:19:39,880 --> 00:19:40,880
so do not worry about a thing.

321
00:19:44,450 --> 00:19:47,020
By the way, Mi Young, why did you do that?

322
00:19:47,460 --> 00:19:49,490
- Excuse me? - The management rights.

323
00:19:50,630 --> 00:19:52,460
Do you really hate the idea of taking them that much?

324
00:19:52,830 --> 00:19:54,430
Yes, I do.

325
00:19:54,500 --> 00:19:57,030
Why? Why do you hate it?

326
00:19:57,100 --> 00:19:59,500
J&White is not just a simple company.

327
00:19:59,570 --> 00:20:00,870
It is a brand.

328
00:20:00,940 --> 00:20:04,410
Every single dress my husband makes is J&White,

329
00:20:04,470 --> 00:20:06,310
and J&White is my husband.

330
00:20:08,110 --> 00:20:09,180
The management rights...

331
00:20:10,180 --> 00:20:11,680
must go to my husband.

332
00:20:13,720 --> 00:20:15,350
What is wrong with everyone today?

333
00:20:15,420 --> 00:20:17,350
Am I the only one who does not understand this situation?

334
00:20:17,420 --> 00:20:19,920
Or am I the weird one?

335
00:20:23,630 --> 00:20:25,730
Anyway, let us eat and gather our strength...

336
00:20:25,800 --> 00:20:27,430
so we can come up with a plan.

337
00:20:29,230 --> 00:20:31,170
That snake...

338
00:20:31,230 --> 00:20:34,640
I am going to turn him into a hagfish.

339
00:20:45,250 --> 00:20:48,090
I thought I was going to die from the cringe.

340
00:20:59,260 --> 00:21:01,330
To generously repay the plaintiff...

341
00:21:01,400 --> 00:21:04,470
for her past devotion.

342
00:21:05,970 --> 00:21:08,170
Who in the world gives away management rights like that?

343
00:21:10,510 --> 00:21:12,940
- Me. - I really...

344
00:21:13,010 --> 00:21:14,580
put on the performance of a lifetime...

345
00:21:14,650 --> 00:21:17,050
just to make you look like a good guy.

346
00:21:17,110 --> 00:21:18,450
You did a very good job.

347
00:21:21,590 --> 00:21:22,590
Right.

348
00:21:22,650 --> 00:21:24,890
Anyway, I am truly grateful for that.

349
00:21:24,960 --> 00:21:27,490
Oh, stop it.

350
00:21:28,530 --> 00:21:31,230
Even if you have no confidence in management,

351
00:21:31,290 --> 00:21:32,900
how could you just hand it all over like this?

352
00:21:35,770 --> 00:21:39,770
Think about it carefully, even now. Are you...

353
00:21:39,840 --> 00:21:41,410
absolutely sure you cannot manage it?

354
00:21:42,810 --> 00:21:44,910
No matter how much I think about it, I cannot do it.

355
00:21:44,980 --> 00:21:48,250
So you are going to hand over management rights no matter what?

356
00:21:50,050 --> 00:21:51,150
Yes.

357
00:21:51,650 --> 00:21:53,620
Until now, everything related to managing the company...

358
00:21:53,680 --> 00:21:55,820
was entirely handled by my wife.

359
00:21:56,320 --> 00:21:58,990
To be honest, I only know how to make dresses.

360
00:21:59,060 --> 00:22:01,690
I know absolutely zero about management.

361
00:22:01,760 --> 00:22:03,830
I have no talent for it and no confidence either.

362
00:22:03,890 --> 00:22:06,130
If we get divorced and my wife leaves the company,

363
00:22:06,200 --> 00:22:08,900
it will only be a matter of time before the company goes under.

364
00:22:08,970 --> 00:22:11,500
So, because you do not want to see the company fail,

365
00:22:11,570 --> 00:22:13,440
you want to hand it over quickly.

366
00:22:15,610 --> 00:22:17,040
This company is like our child.

367
00:22:18,110 --> 00:22:21,140
- One of us has to protect it. - How frustrating.

368
00:22:23,110 --> 00:22:25,320
You should have done better from the start.

369
00:22:27,380 --> 00:22:28,790
Anyway,

370
00:22:29,290 --> 00:22:32,460
persuading her will not be easy. You saw her earlier.

371
00:22:32,520 --> 00:22:33,760
As soon as management rights were mentioned,

372
00:22:33,820 --> 00:22:35,660
she stormed right out.

373
00:22:35,730 --> 00:22:38,830
Then what should we do? Is there any clever solution?

374
00:22:39,860 --> 00:22:40,900
Raise your glass.

375
00:22:43,670 --> 00:22:46,740
Just trust me and wait.

376
00:22:47,340 --> 00:22:49,740
Yes. I will trust you.

377
00:22:54,110 --> 00:22:55,110
Goodness.

378
00:23:45,830 --> 00:23:47,900
Then what is left for you?

379
00:23:47,900 --> 00:23:51,370
If you hand over the company, the only thing you'll get...

380
00:23:51,740 --> 00:23:53,440
after the divorce, what do you plan to do then?

381
00:23:56,710 --> 00:23:58,810
What is the point of a company without you?

382
00:24:01,240 --> 00:24:04,920
As long as I have my skills, I can make dresses anywhere.

383
00:24:04,980 --> 00:24:09,120
There is absolutely no reason why I have to be at J&White.

384
00:24:10,850 --> 00:24:13,090
Then why do I have to be there?

385
00:24:14,490 --> 00:24:16,290
When you are not even there?

386
00:24:31,370 --> 00:24:33,210
Wait, when did you get here?

387
00:24:33,680 --> 00:24:35,950
I was waiting until you finished watering the plants.

388
00:24:39,620 --> 00:24:41,320
Anyway, what brings you here?

389
00:24:41,720 --> 00:24:45,120
- Let us face off like pros. - Face off directly?

390
00:24:45,190 --> 00:24:47,190
Stop playing useless tricks behind my back.

391
00:24:47,260 --> 00:24:49,830
Tricks? What are you talking about?

392
00:24:51,560 --> 00:24:54,630
The divorce trial for the chairman of Yukryong Construction.

393
00:24:56,030 --> 00:24:57,270
You remember it, right?

394
00:25:01,840 --> 00:25:03,270
You should remember it.

395
00:25:03,340 --> 00:25:06,410
- It was the trial of the century. - Are rumors of an affair true?

396
00:25:06,480 --> 00:25:07,740
That trial...

397
00:25:08,380 --> 00:25:10,710
was a lawsuit that would change my life.

398
00:25:10,780 --> 00:25:12,020
Did you know from the beginning?

399
00:25:12,080 --> 00:25:16,020
Divorce trial of the century, with fortunes at stake.

400
00:25:16,090 --> 00:25:19,260
It was. I represented the plaintiff.

401
00:25:19,320 --> 00:25:23,060
And you defended the shameless defendant...

402
00:25:23,130 --> 00:25:25,700
who hid the existence of a child out of wedlock...

403
00:25:25,760 --> 00:25:29,770
- and refused to divorce. - Due to the lack of evidence...

404
00:25:29,830 --> 00:25:32,440
regarding Chairman Yuk's affair and the child out of wedlock,

405
00:25:32,500 --> 00:25:36,340
- I had practically won that trial. - Right.

406
00:25:37,170 --> 00:25:38,170
However...

407
00:25:40,280 --> 00:25:43,350
I call the defendant's driver as a witness.

408
00:25:43,680 --> 00:25:45,480
Hey, you punk.

409
00:25:45,650 --> 00:25:47,280
Is this how you repay my kindness?

410
00:25:48,490 --> 00:25:51,290
- Gosh, Chairman... - Will the child stay quiet?

411
00:25:53,020 --> 00:25:54,160
Darn it.

412
00:25:55,460 --> 00:25:58,400
And to win the trial,

413
00:25:58,460 --> 00:26:02,500
- you threw out a cowardly bait. - A cowardly bait?

414
00:26:02,570 --> 00:26:05,240
I was just faithfully following the trial procedures.

415
00:26:05,540 --> 00:26:08,810
You blindly put someone on the stand without any evidence...

416
00:26:08,870 --> 00:26:10,740
and caused the chairman to have a mental breakdown.

417
00:26:10,810 --> 00:26:13,210
If that is not bait, then what is?

418
00:26:13,280 --> 00:26:17,550
What broke the chairman down was his conscience. Not the bait.

419
00:26:17,950 --> 00:26:21,150
- What did you say? - That is the nature of conscience.

420
00:26:21,480 --> 00:26:25,690
The more you try to cover it up and hide it, the more it squirms.

421
00:26:25,890 --> 00:26:27,160
Twitching like this...

422
00:26:27,220 --> 00:26:28,530
Twitch.

423
00:26:28,590 --> 00:26:30,960
- Is it bait? Or conscience? - What?

424
00:26:31,030 --> 00:26:32,100
Management rights.

425
00:26:33,260 --> 00:26:35,300
No matter how much I think about it, it seems like bait.

426
00:26:36,530 --> 00:26:37,970
If you are that curious,

427
00:26:38,030 --> 00:26:39,400
why don't you just bite it and see?

428
00:26:39,470 --> 00:26:42,440
- Whether it is bait or not. - I cannot do that.

429
00:26:42,510 --> 00:26:44,510
I have already fallen for it once.

430
00:26:45,140 --> 00:26:46,880
All right. Anyway,

431
00:26:47,380 --> 00:26:48,580
let's do our best.

432
00:26:59,690 --> 00:27:00,860
Welcome.

433
00:27:00,920 --> 00:27:03,860
- I want a dress consultation. - Oh, right.

434
00:27:03,930 --> 00:27:05,100
I will guide you this way.

435
00:27:05,160 --> 00:27:07,600
I can consult directly with Designer Ji Won Ho, right?

436
00:27:08,830 --> 00:27:12,740
But CEO Ji is not in right now. Instead, CEO Baek...

437
00:27:12,800 --> 00:27:15,010
Never mind. I will come back next time.

438
00:27:15,640 --> 00:27:17,740
Let's go. Gosh, what a waste of time.

439
00:27:17,810 --> 00:27:18,980
Goodbye.

440
00:27:18,980 --> 00:27:21,280
I will contact you as soon as CEO Ji arrives.

441
00:27:21,340 --> 00:27:22,880
Please make sure to visit us again.

442
00:27:23,880 --> 00:27:25,320
Goodbye.

443
00:27:29,450 --> 00:27:33,220
- How many times has this been? - I know.

444
00:27:33,290 --> 00:27:35,960
Everyone is only looking for CEO Ji today.

445
00:27:37,990 --> 00:27:39,660
Why are you all standing around?

446
00:27:40,400 --> 00:27:42,830
Are the consultations for today's reserved clients already finished?

447
00:27:43,330 --> 00:27:44,330
What?

448
00:27:53,180 --> 00:27:55,610
You are being connected to voicemail...

449
00:27:58,350 --> 00:28:02,250
- Did CEO Ji take the day off? - No, not at all.

450
00:28:03,050 --> 00:28:06,360
Do you think CEO Ji might have gone off the grid?

451
00:28:08,560 --> 00:28:11,160
How many clients came looking for CEO Ji today?

452
00:28:11,230 --> 00:28:13,400
All of them.

453
00:28:13,700 --> 00:28:15,030
All of them?

454
00:28:15,100 --> 00:28:18,700
CEO Ji also has consultations scheduled for the afternoon.

455
00:28:20,200 --> 00:28:22,070
What are we going to do, seriously?

456
00:28:23,440 --> 00:28:25,980
Just one. Oh, darn.

457
00:28:26,040 --> 00:28:29,080
Just one. Come on.

458
00:28:29,150 --> 00:28:30,150
Welcome...

459
00:28:40,360 --> 00:28:42,030
He doesn't want the management rights,

460
00:28:42,190 --> 00:28:43,690
and he is not going to work.

461
00:28:44,730 --> 00:28:46,200
So that is what happened.

462
00:28:46,830 --> 00:28:48,160
No wonder.

463
00:28:48,600 --> 00:28:53,140
Seung Ho, please try to persuade Won Ho.

464
00:28:53,800 --> 00:28:55,770
Even if Won Ho does not listen to anyone else,

465
00:28:55,840 --> 00:28:57,770
he listens to you well.

466
00:28:57,840 --> 00:29:02,780
Once Won Ho makes up his mind, he does not listen to anyone.

467
00:29:02,850 --> 00:29:05,120
But I will try talking to him anyway.

468
00:29:05,180 --> 00:29:06,750
Thank you, Seung Ho.

469
00:29:07,220 --> 00:29:08,220
Mi Young.

470
00:29:09,890 --> 00:29:10,890
Are you okay?

471
00:29:11,450 --> 00:29:14,790
- Sorry? - At least Won Ho has me,

472
00:29:15,190 --> 00:29:18,290
but you do not have any siblings. I was wondering...

473
00:29:18,360 --> 00:29:20,200
who you open up to when you are having a hard time.

474
00:29:21,930 --> 00:29:23,830
Anyway, this punk, Won Ho...

475
00:29:23,900 --> 00:29:26,100
Where did he go instead of going to work?

476
00:29:26,170 --> 00:29:28,470
He is a funny guy, seriously.

477
00:29:28,540 --> 00:29:29,970
I think I know...

478
00:29:31,140 --> 00:29:32,710
where he is.

479
00:29:34,010 --> 00:29:38,450
Today, we are going to draw our favorite things.

480
00:29:39,520 --> 00:29:41,520
- Is anyone done with drawing? - I am.

481
00:29:41,520 --> 00:29:42,690
Oh, are you finished?

482
00:29:42,750 --> 00:29:45,620
- Yes. - Let me see. Let's see.

483
00:29:45,890 --> 00:29:47,590
Goodness!

484
00:29:47,690 --> 00:29:49,890
- I drew it well, right? - Are these two friends?

485
00:29:49,960 --> 00:29:52,260
Yes. This is Wenda.

486
00:29:52,330 --> 00:29:54,800
- But how should we color... - Wenda?

487
00:29:54,860 --> 00:29:56,500
- She is silver, though? - Oh, is she?

488
00:29:56,570 --> 00:29:57,570
Let's try it anyway.

489
00:29:58,900 --> 00:30:01,070
What color should we use? Black?

490
00:30:01,640 --> 00:30:02,740
Okay.

491
00:30:03,270 --> 00:30:04,970
What color are you going to make Wenda?

492
00:30:06,210 --> 00:30:07,940
She is originally white.

493
00:30:18,860 --> 00:30:20,620
How did you know I was here?

494
00:30:20,690 --> 00:30:22,890
Where else would you go other than the motel?

495
00:30:24,390 --> 00:30:26,400
What are you doing here right now?

496
00:30:26,460 --> 00:30:29,300
Volunteer work. I told Father Kwon that for a while,

497
00:30:29,330 --> 00:30:31,430
I would watch the kids here.

498
00:30:31,940 --> 00:30:34,170
That darn volunteer work, seriously.

499
00:30:34,700 --> 00:30:36,810
Won Ho, you are the CEO of the company.

500
00:30:36,870 --> 00:30:38,780
For a CEO to be so irresponsible!

501
00:30:38,840 --> 00:30:40,880
Are you not embarrassed to face the employees?

502
00:30:40,940 --> 00:30:42,750
That is why I am not going to do it anymore.

503
00:30:42,810 --> 00:30:43,810
What?

504
00:30:45,420 --> 00:30:48,120
From today on, you be the CEO alone.

505
00:30:48,250 --> 00:30:50,950
- Alone? - I am handing over management.

506
00:30:51,520 --> 00:30:53,160
Starting today, I will let you do...

507
00:30:53,220 --> 00:30:54,790
the thing you do best to your heart's content.

508
00:30:56,060 --> 00:30:58,490
I will not argue or get in your way,

509
00:30:58,560 --> 00:31:00,560
so you take charge of J&White and do a good job.

510
00:31:00,630 --> 00:31:03,670
- You are really not going to argue? - Of course not.

511
00:31:04,000 --> 00:31:06,200
From now on, I will follow your opinions unconditionally.

512
00:31:06,700 --> 00:31:07,970
Understood.

513
00:31:08,670 --> 00:31:11,440
- Okay. - Then I am quitting the company.

514
00:31:12,010 --> 00:31:13,010
What?

515
00:31:14,440 --> 00:31:16,250
What if my husband...

516
00:31:16,310 --> 00:31:18,920
insists on giving me the management rights until the end?

517
00:31:18,980 --> 00:31:20,480
We have to show him too.

518
00:31:20,950 --> 00:31:22,320
If they are going to be stubborn,

519
00:31:22,390 --> 00:31:24,390
you have to be even more stubborn.

520
00:31:24,790 --> 00:31:26,360
Fight fire with fire.

521
00:31:26,920 --> 00:31:28,490
From this moment on,

522
00:31:28,690 --> 00:31:31,360
I am completely cutting ties with J&White.

523
00:31:32,130 --> 00:31:33,160
What do you mean, cutting ties?

524
00:31:33,230 --> 00:31:34,500
What are you talking about all of a sudden?

525
00:31:34,830 --> 00:31:36,530
Who will mind the company?

526
00:31:36,570 --> 00:31:38,530
If you're worried, you go and check.

527
00:31:40,400 --> 00:31:41,740
Seriously...

528
00:31:43,840 --> 00:31:46,410
In order to avoid dividing assets with the plaintiff,

529
00:31:46,480 --> 00:31:48,950
the defendant is abusing management rights of the company,

530
00:31:49,010 --> 00:31:51,510
and the grounds for this are as follows.

531
00:31:51,580 --> 00:31:53,680
What, 790,00 dollars for the asset division?

532
00:31:53,750 --> 00:31:56,290
- Is 790,000 a joke to you? - So?

533
00:31:56,350 --> 00:31:59,060
- You refuse to give it? - I cannot give it,

534
00:31:59,120 --> 00:32:00,560
so just do it by the book

535
00:32:00,620 --> 00:32:01,790
First,

536
00:32:01,860 --> 00:32:04,930
regarding the plaintiff's demands for asset division,

537
00:32:04,990 --> 00:32:07,160
the defendant has never agreed to them...

538
00:32:07,230 --> 00:32:09,700
and has instead strongly opposed them.

539
00:32:09,770 --> 00:32:11,270
Stop acting like you know everything.

540
00:32:11,330 --> 00:32:12,740
Is the company yours or something?

541
00:32:12,800 --> 00:32:14,770
- Second. - Yes.

542
00:32:14,840 --> 00:32:17,670
Due to differences in opinion regarding company matters,

543
00:32:17,740 --> 00:32:19,740
the defendant frequently clashed with the plaintiff.

544
00:32:22,050 --> 00:32:23,650
Furthermore, he always emphasized to the plaintiff...

545
00:32:23,710 --> 00:32:28,120
that the company's identity belonged to the defendant.

546
00:32:28,180 --> 00:32:31,220
Just use this. I bought some of this today.

547
00:32:31,290 --> 00:32:32,490
- Oh, my. - Here.

548
00:32:33,490 --> 00:32:36,290
- The preparatory brief has arrived. - Oh, it is here already?

549
00:32:37,830 --> 00:32:38,930
Only one page came?

550
00:32:40,460 --> 00:32:42,370
Judging from these circumstances,

551
00:32:42,900 --> 00:32:44,870
the defendant's intent to hand over management rights...

552
00:32:44,870 --> 00:32:46,440
to the plaintiff...

553
00:32:46,500 --> 00:32:50,140
cannot be seen as pure, and therefore, the plaintiff...

554
00:32:50,210 --> 00:32:52,980
cannot accept the defendant's demands.

555
00:32:53,040 --> 00:32:54,510
What do you mean, it cannot be seen as pure?

556
00:32:54,580 --> 00:32:55,910
What is this nonsense?

557
00:32:56,710 --> 00:32:59,050
You told me to just trust you!

558
00:33:02,420 --> 00:33:04,150
It is not as easy as I thought.

559
00:33:05,150 --> 00:33:06,320
Seriously.

560
00:33:06,860 --> 00:33:08,190
If this keeps up and my wife...

561
00:33:08,260 --> 00:33:10,460
refuses to take management rights, what will you do?

562
00:33:10,530 --> 00:33:14,230
Then what else can we do? We will have to force it on her.

563
00:33:14,300 --> 00:33:17,470
- What? - Wait. I knew this would happen,

564
00:33:17,530 --> 00:33:20,240
so I set a little trap.

565
00:33:21,000 --> 00:33:22,440
A trap?

566
00:33:22,510 --> 00:33:25,410
Smoke to lure the tiger out of its cave.

567
00:33:27,880 --> 00:33:31,780
It is about time for a bite.

568
00:33:37,220 --> 00:33:38,420
Yes, Manager Song.

569
00:33:38,960 --> 00:33:42,730
- Is it true? - So unlucky. We want a refund!

570
00:33:46,530 --> 00:33:48,060
Give us a refund!

571
00:33:48,130 --> 00:33:51,630
CEO Ji, where are you? Customers are here,

572
00:33:51,700 --> 00:33:53,600
and they are making a huge fuss.

573
00:33:53,600 --> 00:33:55,000
What?

574
00:33:55,070 --> 00:33:57,540
Okay, I understand. I will be right there.

575
00:33:57,970 --> 00:34:00,610
- What is happening all of a sudden? - I told you, right?

576
00:34:01,080 --> 00:34:02,480
That we would get a bite.

577
00:34:03,680 --> 00:34:06,150
What? Did you do this?

578
00:34:06,520 --> 00:34:10,050
- What on earth did you do? - I just...

579
00:34:10,850 --> 00:34:13,820
posted a promotional message on the local moms' forum.

580
00:34:14,360 --> 00:34:16,430
"Even if we are getting divorced soon,"

581
00:34:16,490 --> 00:34:20,400
"please support and show interest in J&White."

582
00:34:20,900 --> 00:34:22,130
What did you say?

583
00:34:22,200 --> 00:34:25,740
Just wait. Your wife will be at the company soon.

584
00:34:26,370 --> 00:34:31,310
I seriously cannot deal with this. Darn. See you later.

585
00:34:32,640 --> 00:34:35,610
That guy... I told him to temper his anger.

586
00:34:36,880 --> 00:34:39,150
A refund will be difficult, ma'am.

587
00:34:39,220 --> 00:34:42,190
Ma'am, cancellation as of today is not possible.

588
00:34:42,250 --> 00:34:44,520
Given that the wedding shop caters to...

589
00:34:44,590 --> 00:34:46,320
prospective couples about to get married,

590
00:34:46,390 --> 00:34:49,930
plaintiff Baek Mi Young and defendant Ji Won Ho's divorce,

591
00:34:49,990 --> 00:34:54,600
is bound to have a negative impact on the company's reputation.

592
00:34:55,030 --> 00:34:56,270
(They were a couple who were married in name only?)

593
00:34:56,330 --> 00:34:58,170
(A wedding shop couple getting divorced?)

594
00:34:58,230 --> 00:34:59,340
(I got my dress there.)

595
00:34:59,400 --> 00:35:00,940
(I'm completely ruined.)

596
00:35:03,910 --> 00:35:05,740
(How can we trust them with our wedding dresses?)

597
00:35:10,250 --> 00:35:11,310
Let me see...

598
00:35:16,090 --> 00:35:18,090
The male CEO...

599
00:35:18,150 --> 00:35:20,960
from here...

600
00:35:21,020 --> 00:35:22,330
is a total...

601
00:35:22,390 --> 00:35:23,860
huge...

602
00:35:23,930 --> 00:35:25,560
jerk.

603
00:35:33,470 --> 00:35:34,540
Furthermore,

604
00:35:34,600 --> 00:35:36,310
the plaintiff, who has operated the company...

605
00:35:36,370 --> 00:35:38,710
with outstanding management skills...

606
00:35:38,770 --> 00:35:42,280
Could she really have been unaware of the impact...

607
00:35:42,750 --> 00:35:44,210
their divorce would have on the company?

608
00:35:47,020 --> 00:35:48,520
(Song A Ri)

609
00:35:52,790 --> 00:35:54,020
Yes, A Ri.

610
00:35:54,090 --> 00:35:56,360
If the plaintiff, who treated the company like her own child...

611
00:35:56,430 --> 00:35:59,930
and dedicated herself to it,

612
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:04,200
ignores this crisis...

613
00:36:04,270 --> 00:36:07,440
and only demands property division,

614
00:36:07,500 --> 00:36:10,370
would that not be too selfish of an action?

615
00:36:12,210 --> 00:36:13,610
Bring out the CEO!

616
00:36:15,580 --> 00:36:19,480
Like the defendant who gave up management for the plaintiff,

617
00:36:21,180 --> 00:36:24,150
we hope the plaintiff will also...

618
00:36:24,220 --> 00:36:26,620
make a decision for the sake of the company.

619
00:36:27,190 --> 00:36:29,290
For the company, the plaintiff, the defendant,

620
00:36:29,360 --> 00:36:32,830
and for the peace of everyone involved.

621
00:36:34,130 --> 00:36:37,200
How about focusing on the dresses, regardless of the divorce?

622
00:36:38,270 --> 00:36:41,300
The dresses have nothing to do with your personal lives.

623
00:36:41,370 --> 00:36:43,110
(Baek Mi Young)

624
00:36:44,110 --> 00:36:45,210
Are you the CEO?

625
00:36:52,350 --> 00:36:53,350
(Lawyer Jeon Chi Hyun)

626
00:36:54,320 --> 00:36:57,050
- Yes, Lawyer Jeon. - Mi Young, what are you doing?

627
00:36:57,120 --> 00:36:58,520
Are you enjoying your well-deserved rest?

628
00:36:59,220 --> 00:37:00,420
Yes.

629
00:37:00,490 --> 00:37:04,530
But I saw a post on the moms' forum.

630
00:37:04,560 --> 00:37:06,800
A post? What kind of post?

631
00:37:06,930 --> 00:37:09,500
It was talking about my husband and me getting a divorce.

632
00:37:09,570 --> 00:37:12,340
And because wedding shop CEOs are getting divorced,

633
00:37:13,540 --> 00:37:16,040
there were so many negative comments.

634
00:37:16,110 --> 00:37:19,880
- That is all snake's doing. - What?

635
00:37:19,940 --> 00:37:23,110
Mi Young, you absolutely must not respond, understood?

636
00:37:23,880 --> 00:37:26,850
From now on, you have nothing to do with the company.

637
00:37:27,280 --> 00:37:30,220
Oh, okay, I will keep that in mind.

638
00:37:38,560 --> 00:37:40,860
Because of the dress you made,

639
00:37:41,300 --> 00:37:43,400
my wedding was ruined,

640
00:37:43,800 --> 00:37:47,270
so you need to pay for the dress and compensate my distress.

641
00:37:47,340 --> 00:37:50,070
You say your wedding was ruined because of my dress?

642
00:37:50,240 --> 00:37:52,840
Of course it is because of you. A guy who is about to get divorced...

643
00:37:52,910 --> 00:37:56,180
- has no business making dresses. - Excuse me?

644
00:37:56,310 --> 00:37:59,020
- Are you done talking? - No, I am not. Why?

645
00:37:59,080 --> 00:38:01,120
Oh, seriously, do you think I am an idiot?

646
00:38:01,180 --> 00:38:03,250
CEO Ji, please hold back. You cannot do this.

647
00:38:03,990 --> 00:38:06,820
You better leave before I call the police.

648
00:38:07,120 --> 00:38:08,820
So you are saying you will not pay me?

649
00:38:08,890 --> 00:38:10,990
Why would I pay you? Get out right now!

650
00:38:15,600 --> 00:38:16,600
Come in.

651
00:38:22,540 --> 00:38:23,540
What is going on?

652
00:38:26,940 --> 00:38:27,940
What are you waiting for?

653
00:38:29,350 --> 00:38:30,350
- Yes, sir. - Yes, sir.

654
00:38:37,350 --> 00:38:38,350
Move!

655
00:38:40,160 --> 00:38:42,730
Who are you people? Stop this right now!

656
00:38:42,790 --> 00:38:44,290
You talk to me.

657
00:38:45,390 --> 00:38:46,400
What?

658
00:38:53,370 --> 00:38:54,370
Hurry up.

659
00:39:10,590 --> 00:39:13,090
What? It's not even 12pm.

660
00:39:25,970 --> 00:39:28,200
(Song A Ri)

661
00:39:31,540 --> 00:39:35,110
- Are you going to pay me or not? - You should be paying.

662
00:39:35,180 --> 00:39:36,180
What?

663
00:39:36,250 --> 00:39:38,250
For trashing our shop like this, I'm going to sue you...

664
00:39:38,310 --> 00:39:39,880
for all the damages. Got it?

665
00:39:39,950 --> 00:39:41,680
You still haven't come to your senses.

666
00:39:41,750 --> 00:39:42,990
Stop it, you jerks.

667
00:39:45,820 --> 00:39:47,260
- Mi Young! - Mi Young, it's dangerous.

668
00:39:47,260 --> 00:39:48,320
Get out of here.

669
00:39:50,090 --> 00:39:51,560
Darn it.

670
00:39:51,630 --> 00:39:55,160
- Who is this now? - Did you trash our shop?

671
00:39:55,230 --> 00:39:57,730
Yes, we did it. Why? What are you going to do about it?

672
00:39:57,800 --> 00:39:59,200
I might let other things slide,

673
00:39:59,270 --> 00:40:01,870
but I will not tolerate you ruining J&White like this.

674
00:40:01,940 --> 00:40:04,870
- And what if you don't tolerate it? - What am I going to do?

675
00:40:08,810 --> 00:40:10,410
What the hell?

676
00:40:10,480 --> 00:40:12,310
Hey, grab her.

677
00:40:12,380 --> 00:40:13,780
Grab her!

678
00:40:13,850 --> 00:40:15,820
- Stop it! - Darn it!

679
00:40:17,150 --> 00:40:21,090
- Darn. Have you lost your mind? - Hit me. I dare you to hit me.

680
00:40:21,160 --> 00:40:22,490
You think I won't?

681
00:40:22,560 --> 00:40:23,560
Hey!

682
00:40:33,400 --> 00:40:36,040
Have we met somewhere before?

683
00:40:36,470 --> 00:40:38,140
Why do you look so familiar?

684
00:40:38,640 --> 00:40:39,780
I know, right?

685
00:40:40,440 --> 00:40:42,580
You look familiar to me too.

686
00:40:43,710 --> 00:40:45,880
Where have we seen each other?

687
00:40:47,050 --> 00:40:51,190
Do you happen to know Bok Soon from Hwasun?

688
00:40:51,750 --> 00:40:52,960
Bok Soon?

689
00:40:54,020 --> 00:40:57,260
- Oh, Jeong Bok Soon? - Yes, that is right.

690
00:40:57,330 --> 00:41:00,660
You helped with Jeong Bok Soon's free wedding five years ago.

691
00:41:01,160 --> 00:41:04,500
I am Jeong Bok Soon's younger brother.

692
00:41:04,570 --> 00:41:06,440
- Jeong Bok Soon's brother? - Yes.

693
00:41:06,440 --> 00:41:07,840
Long time no see!

694
00:41:08,240 --> 00:41:11,310
Gosh, I mean, what are the odds?

695
00:41:11,470 --> 00:41:14,080
- I know, right? - What are you doing? Say hello.

696
00:41:14,140 --> 00:41:16,310
This is the person who, when our family was struggling,

697
00:41:16,380 --> 00:41:19,450
helped our sister's free wedding. She is our savior.

698
00:41:19,520 --> 00:41:20,720
- Hello! - Hello!

699
00:41:22,450 --> 00:41:25,290
Oh, no need for formalities. But...

700
00:41:26,220 --> 00:41:28,390
Gosh, that is a bit of a problem.

701
00:41:28,460 --> 00:41:30,330
Oh, we are sorry.

702
00:41:30,390 --> 00:41:31,860
- We are sorry! - We are sorry!

703
00:41:32,290 --> 00:41:35,030
I did not know you were our savior, and I was so disrespectful.

704
00:41:36,830 --> 00:41:38,270
Hey, what are you doing? Clean it up quickly.

705
00:41:38,330 --> 00:41:39,640
- Yes, sir. - Clean it up.

706
00:41:39,640 --> 00:41:41,240
Clean it up quickly.

707
00:41:41,300 --> 00:41:43,570
- Clean it up. - Oh, I am sorry too.

708
00:41:43,640 --> 00:41:45,010
Oh, what should we do?

709
00:41:45,070 --> 00:41:46,380
You are wearing such a nice suit too.

710
00:41:49,550 --> 00:41:52,550
- Goodness! - I am sorry, this safety pin...

711
00:41:52,620 --> 00:41:54,380
Oh, it is okay.

712
00:41:58,350 --> 00:42:00,560
- It is right here. - Oh, yes.

713
00:42:00,620 --> 00:42:03,330
Here too. Do not leave any behind.

714
00:42:05,790 --> 00:42:09,430
- Please be careful. It is costly. - Oh, yes.

715
00:42:09,700 --> 00:42:12,100
Over here, scrub it hard over here.

716
00:42:14,140 --> 00:42:16,170
- Scrub it hard. - Yes.

717
00:42:16,240 --> 00:42:17,740
Scrub it. That's right.

718
00:42:19,980 --> 00:42:22,610
How is it? Is there anything else you need?

719
00:42:22,850 --> 00:42:24,850
Oh, there are some stones fallen over here.

720
00:42:24,910 --> 00:42:27,880
Oh, the stones here. Gyeong Won, give it to me.

721
00:42:36,090 --> 00:42:37,460
(J&White Wedding)

722
00:42:48,300 --> 00:42:50,140
When did you volunteer to do free weddings?

723
00:42:50,210 --> 00:42:51,810
Without even telling me?

724
00:42:51,870 --> 00:42:55,310
You always nagged me about doing volunteer work. Goodness.

725
00:42:55,380 --> 00:42:56,810
What is so funny?

726
00:42:57,450 --> 00:42:58,450
What? Nothing.

727
00:43:00,080 --> 00:43:03,190
Anyway, this makes everything clear.

728
00:43:04,750 --> 00:43:07,520
It is only right that you take over management of the company.

729
00:43:07,590 --> 00:43:08,590
What?

730
00:43:08,660 --> 00:43:11,830
You always end up saving J&White whenever there is a crisis.

731
00:43:12,330 --> 00:43:15,030
At this point, we should pretty much consider it destiny, should we not?

732
00:43:15,100 --> 00:43:16,670
You seem pretty excited about this.

733
00:43:17,130 --> 00:43:20,170
- What? - Dumping the company on me...

734
00:43:20,770 --> 00:43:22,740
must make you feel relieved already.

735
00:43:23,070 --> 00:43:25,980
Oh, come on, why would you say it like that?

736
00:43:26,510 --> 00:43:27,940
Then how am I supposed to forget?

737
00:43:29,280 --> 00:43:31,580
It is easy for you to just up and leave,

738
00:43:32,880 --> 00:43:35,020
but I have to stay here.

739
00:43:35,750 --> 00:43:37,650
The entirety of J&White...

740
00:43:37,720 --> 00:43:39,660
is filled with traces of you,

741
00:43:40,520 --> 00:43:41,520
so how am I...

742
00:43:43,230 --> 00:43:45,130
supposed to erase you?

743
00:43:49,130 --> 00:43:50,130
Mi Young.

744
00:43:50,730 --> 00:43:52,270
I am not confident I can do it alone.

745
00:43:58,470 --> 00:44:00,280
I am not confident either, Mi Young.

746
00:44:01,340 --> 00:44:03,410
Honestly, I am so embarrassed to say this.

747
00:44:05,350 --> 00:44:08,450
I am actually terrified that I will ruin the company without you.

748
00:44:09,620 --> 00:44:13,120
I am so scared that I do not even dare...

749
00:44:14,460 --> 00:44:15,960
to try running the company on my own.

750
00:44:21,030 --> 00:44:22,600
But you are different from me.

751
00:44:23,900 --> 00:44:25,000
You are brave.

752
00:44:26,300 --> 00:44:28,000
You put up with a guy like me for seven years,

753
00:44:28,070 --> 00:44:29,740
so you are a truly amazing person...

754
00:44:30,970 --> 00:44:32,840
and an amazing woman.

755
00:44:32,910 --> 00:44:35,640
Even I think that is pretty amazing.

756
00:44:44,220 --> 00:44:45,220
Our child...

757
00:44:47,490 --> 00:44:49,360
You can take responsibility and raise it well, right?

758
00:44:55,530 --> 00:44:58,130
I am always shamelessly asking you for favors like this.

759
00:44:59,330 --> 00:45:00,340
I am sorry.

760
00:45:01,970 --> 00:45:03,010
Do you even know what you're sorry for?

761
00:45:07,910 --> 00:45:09,010
As long as you know, it's fine.

762
00:45:23,430 --> 00:45:25,160
(Yeonnam Family Court)

763
00:45:25,230 --> 00:45:28,460
The plaintiff accepts the defendant's proposal, correct?

764
00:45:32,600 --> 00:45:33,600
Yes.

765
00:45:34,900 --> 00:45:38,340
Defendant, is it okay to conclude the mediation like this?

766
00:45:42,180 --> 00:45:43,350
Yes.

767
00:45:43,410 --> 00:45:45,910
Then I will call the judge right away.

768
00:46:17,150 --> 00:46:19,850
Mediation has the same effect as a final judgment,

769
00:46:19,920 --> 00:46:23,350
and I confirm the mediation between both parties has been established.

770
00:46:29,560 --> 00:46:32,530
The plaintiff and defendant are divorced.

771
00:46:42,070 --> 00:46:44,610
Oh, my.

772
00:46:44,970 --> 00:46:47,880
Well, it ended like this for you two.

773
00:46:49,240 --> 00:46:51,080
Meeting like this is fate too.

774
00:46:51,150 --> 00:46:53,850
How about soft tofu stew at the place by the intersection...

775
00:46:53,920 --> 00:46:56,920
The two of us should leave.

776
00:46:58,320 --> 00:47:01,160
Oh, I suppose we should.

777
00:47:01,220 --> 00:47:02,220
Yes.

778
00:47:03,790 --> 00:47:04,790
Yes, well then.

779
00:47:16,270 --> 00:47:17,810
(Yeonnam Family Court)

780
00:47:22,740 --> 00:47:24,050
What was it this time?

781
00:47:27,750 --> 00:47:28,880
Bait and conscience.

782
00:47:30,290 --> 00:47:32,320
Which one did you use to hook them?

783
00:47:32,390 --> 00:47:34,820
Do you still think you lost?

784
00:47:34,890 --> 00:47:36,890
Then did you lose?

785
00:47:36,960 --> 00:47:37,960
No.

786
00:47:40,060 --> 00:47:42,930
But I don't feel like I won, either.

787
00:47:43,500 --> 00:47:44,900
Telepathy.

788
00:47:45,900 --> 00:47:48,370
- What? - Neither bait nor conscience...

789
00:47:49,970 --> 00:47:51,510
but telepathy.

790
00:48:16,570 --> 00:48:17,570
What?

791
00:48:27,240 --> 00:48:30,180
I really don't know what to say at a time like this.

792
00:48:31,250 --> 00:48:32,250
I know.

793
00:48:33,350 --> 00:48:35,620
It's cliche, but only one thing comes to mind.

794
00:48:38,890 --> 00:48:40,420
Take care of yourself.

795
00:48:40,990 --> 00:48:41,990
Don't get sick.

796
00:48:43,130 --> 00:48:44,130
You too, Won Ho.

797
00:48:46,830 --> 00:48:47,830
Then...

798
00:48:49,460 --> 00:48:53,700
it's cliche, but should we shake hands one last time?

799
00:49:02,540 --> 00:49:04,080
Goodbye, Ji Won Ho.

800
00:49:05,510 --> 00:49:07,950
Goodbye, Mi Young.

801
00:49:19,760 --> 00:49:23,600
(1 year later)

802
00:49:25,000 --> 00:49:28,300
- Hello. Right this way. - Okay. It's that way.

803
00:49:37,380 --> 00:49:38,380
Vice President Song.

804
00:49:41,720 --> 00:49:44,150
- Yes? - The fabric arrived.

805
00:49:44,220 --> 00:49:45,920
Oh, hold on.

806
00:49:46,560 --> 00:49:48,790
Ma'am, I'll call you back.

807
00:49:51,190 --> 00:49:53,560
- Please take a look for a moment. - Okay.

808
00:49:55,860 --> 00:49:57,530
- Welcome. - Hello.

809
00:49:57,600 --> 00:50:00,200
Is a consultation possible with the CEO today?

810
00:50:00,270 --> 00:50:02,140
Oh, the CEO?

811
00:50:02,200 --> 00:50:05,010
The CEO is out for a moment right now.

812
00:50:05,170 --> 00:50:07,940
I'm the Vice President, though.

813
00:50:08,240 --> 00:50:09,340
Vice President...

814
00:50:13,220 --> 00:50:15,250
Oh, yes, um, just a moment.

815
00:50:16,250 --> 00:50:17,620
(Baek Mi Young)

816
00:50:22,390 --> 00:50:23,660
(Song A Ri)

817
00:50:29,970 --> 00:50:32,230
Shouldn't you answer that?

818
00:50:32,300 --> 00:50:34,840
Don't worry about it and just answer my question.

819
00:50:34,900 --> 00:50:36,540
You're the one who poached my designer, right?

820
00:50:36,610 --> 00:50:38,710
Poached? No way.

821
00:50:38,770 --> 00:50:41,940
- I officially scouted them. - That's the same thing.

822
00:50:42,080 --> 00:50:43,310
Whatever.

823
00:50:43,780 --> 00:50:45,610
- Give them back right now. - Give you back what?

824
00:50:45,680 --> 00:50:49,080
Put my designer back where they belong right now.

825
00:50:49,250 --> 00:50:52,390
Do you know how much effort I put into bringing that designer in?

826
00:50:52,990 --> 00:50:55,460
I don't know exactly how much effort that was,

827
00:50:55,960 --> 00:50:58,660
but I probably added another zero to it.

828
00:50:58,730 --> 00:50:59,930
Hey, Calvin.

829
00:51:00,000 --> 00:51:03,030
Sorry, but that is water under the bridge.

830
00:51:03,600 --> 00:51:07,440
I made an official offer, and your designer accepted it.

831
00:51:10,570 --> 00:51:13,280
Come on, do not be like that. You are Calvin.

832
00:51:13,340 --> 00:51:16,650
You can find a much better designer whenever you want.

833
00:51:16,710 --> 00:51:18,010
Okay? Please.

834
00:51:28,590 --> 00:51:30,330
No, I cannot give them back.

835
00:51:31,830 --> 00:51:33,460
It is hard to find a good designer these days.

836
00:51:33,530 --> 00:51:35,630
That is why I worked so hard to bring them in.

837
00:51:35,700 --> 00:51:39,330
Help me out a little. Please? Come on.

838
00:51:41,840 --> 00:51:43,100
Get a grip.

839
00:51:43,170 --> 00:51:46,680
- No. - Oh, come on, please help me out.

840
00:51:46,740 --> 00:51:49,440
- I am having a hard time. - Then give me money.

841
00:51:49,510 --> 00:51:51,950
- You are so cheap, seriously. - You do not want to do that, right?

842
00:51:52,010 --> 00:51:53,010
Yes.

843
00:51:53,080 --> 00:51:56,720
- Hey, please. - No way.

844
00:51:56,790 --> 00:51:57,990
Goodness.

845
00:51:58,050 --> 00:52:01,760
- It was hard to hire them. - Where is this audacity from?

846
00:52:08,760 --> 00:52:10,330
Calvin, that jerk...

847
00:52:10,400 --> 00:52:12,230
How can he be so shameless?

848
00:52:12,300 --> 00:52:14,770
After all those times he bent over backward for you.

849
00:52:14,840 --> 00:52:17,040
This is why you should never trust men.

850
00:52:17,110 --> 00:52:20,210
Anyway, where are we going to find another designer?

851
00:52:20,280 --> 00:52:23,250
I know, they did not even last a month this time.

852
00:52:24,380 --> 00:52:27,480
But why do the designers keep leaving?

853
00:52:27,550 --> 00:52:29,580
What do you think the reason is?

854
00:52:29,650 --> 00:52:31,350
Why in the world could it be?

855
00:52:33,420 --> 00:52:35,460
- Well? - What?

856
00:52:35,520 --> 00:52:39,130
- Is it because of me? - Honestly, you're really picky.

857
00:52:39,190 --> 00:52:41,130
You cannot tolerate even a single mistake.

858
00:52:41,200 --> 00:52:42,400
You are an extreme perfectionist.

859
00:52:44,470 --> 00:52:45,470
Was I?

860
00:52:46,470 --> 00:52:49,500
- I cannot do things half-heartedly. - So, then...

861
00:52:50,040 --> 00:52:51,740
should I post the job opening again?

862
00:52:52,270 --> 00:52:56,980
We have to. Oh, with a higher salary this time?

863
00:52:57,250 --> 00:52:59,780
Goodness. Fine.

864
00:53:02,450 --> 00:53:03,720
- Welcome. - Welcome.

865
00:53:12,060 --> 00:53:13,400
Yes, this is Baek Mi Young.

866
00:53:14,600 --> 00:53:17,200
- Oh, yes. - I, Baek Mi Young...

867
00:53:18,600 --> 00:53:19,970
My life after divorce...

868
00:53:21,970 --> 00:53:23,740
is still tough.

869
00:53:24,240 --> 00:53:27,780
Worries and chores pile up like a mountain,

870
00:53:28,240 --> 00:53:32,180
and now I have to face all of this all by myself.

871
00:53:32,250 --> 00:53:34,420
For those of you who think you have a round face,

872
00:53:34,480 --> 00:53:36,120
it is better to leave it open.

873
00:53:37,520 --> 00:53:38,820
However, I...

874
00:53:38,890 --> 00:53:40,560
already know from experience.

875
00:53:42,320 --> 00:53:43,990
That this hardship right now...

876
00:53:44,560 --> 00:53:47,400
is just a passing season anyway.

877
00:53:53,470 --> 00:53:55,470
Is it possible to come to work in the afternoon?

878
00:53:55,540 --> 00:53:57,510
I have a hard time waking up in the morning.

879
00:53:57,570 --> 00:53:59,810
I can use my vacation days however I want, right?

880
00:53:59,870 --> 00:54:01,610
Do places like this give performance bonuses?

881
00:54:01,680 --> 00:54:04,210
I do not think this is a good fit for me.

882
00:54:04,280 --> 00:54:06,250
Is there a separate snack time?

883
00:54:07,450 --> 00:54:09,550
You have to deal with customers all day,

884
00:54:09,620 --> 00:54:11,150
and you want to be eating snacks constantly?

885
00:54:11,720 --> 00:54:13,250
(CEO Baek Mi Young)

886
00:54:25,130 --> 00:54:26,940
If I endure this winter,

887
00:54:28,000 --> 00:54:31,310
spring will surely come.

888
00:55:29,500 --> 00:55:32,600
There is nothing special today.

889
00:55:32,670 --> 00:55:34,640
Really? I think it is very interesting.

890
00:55:34,840 --> 00:55:38,770
- Stop staring. It will wear out. - No, I am going to keep looking.

891
00:55:39,170 --> 00:55:42,080
How can I never get tired of looking at your face, honey?

892
00:55:42,140 --> 00:55:43,810
Oh, what is wrong with you?

893
00:55:43,880 --> 00:55:47,020
- Stop joking around. - I am not joking. I am serious.

894
00:55:47,080 --> 00:55:48,850
Oh, you did not even put anything on your face,

895
00:55:48,920 --> 00:55:50,950
but how is it glowing like this?

896
00:55:51,550 --> 00:55:52,790
Gosh, it is blinding.

897
00:55:54,360 --> 00:55:57,090
- I did! - What?

898
00:55:57,160 --> 00:55:58,330
No, you did not.

899
00:56:00,800 --> 00:56:03,160
- Anyway, you are really pretty. - What is so funny?

900
00:56:04,570 --> 00:56:05,830
Hello.

901
00:56:06,330 --> 00:56:07,540
I see you often.

902
00:56:08,070 --> 00:56:11,870
- I saw you seven times this week. - Oh, you are right.

903
00:56:19,380 --> 00:56:20,380
Stop it.

904
00:56:28,920 --> 00:56:29,920
Goodbye.

905
00:56:33,900 --> 00:56:35,060
What is it?

906
00:56:35,130 --> 00:56:38,070
- What are you two doing right now? - Oh, it is just a thing.

907
00:56:39,600 --> 00:56:40,970
You do not need to know, Mom.

908
00:56:41,040 --> 00:56:43,000
Gosh, why do you want to know everything?

909
00:56:43,070 --> 00:56:44,440
Are you having fun?

910
00:56:44,870 --> 00:56:46,210
What's wrong?

911
00:56:46,270 --> 00:56:48,240
If you are jealous, you should date someone too.

912
00:56:48,310 --> 00:56:51,250
Gosh, dating, my foot.

913
00:56:52,010 --> 00:56:54,950
By the way, have you heard anything from Won Ho?

914
00:56:55,020 --> 00:56:56,920
Won Ho? No, I have not.

915
00:56:57,320 --> 00:56:59,790
Gosh, if Won Ho is doing well, he should say so.

916
00:56:59,850 --> 00:57:01,290
He should at least call.

917
00:57:01,360 --> 00:57:04,290
I do not even know if he is dead or alive.

918
00:57:04,360 --> 00:57:05,660
Do not worry, Mom.

919
00:57:05,730 --> 00:57:10,060
- No news is good news. - Must be nice to be carefree.

920
00:57:14,940 --> 00:57:16,870
You are saying the Azalea bloomed?

921
00:57:16,940 --> 00:57:19,710
I am telling you. And in full bloom too.

922
00:57:22,580 --> 00:57:23,580
(CEO Baek Mi Young)

923
00:57:24,150 --> 00:57:26,250
Look, I am right, aren't I?

924
00:57:26,310 --> 00:57:28,880
Oh, my. You were right.

925
00:57:29,280 --> 00:57:31,120
But the weather has not even warmed up yet,

926
00:57:31,190 --> 00:57:32,650
how did it bloom so fast?

927
00:57:32,720 --> 00:57:34,990
Exactly. It is so amazing.

928
00:57:36,060 --> 00:57:38,990
Hey, I have a good feeling about this.

929
00:57:40,230 --> 00:57:42,930
They are definitely coming today.

930
00:57:43,360 --> 00:57:46,130
- What? - The designer, I mean.

931
00:57:46,670 --> 00:57:47,670
I feel...

932
00:57:47,740 --> 00:57:50,940
a really great person is going to come today.

933
00:57:51,010 --> 00:57:52,240
I can just feel it.

934
00:57:52,310 --> 00:57:55,240
- You can just feel it? - I am telling you.

935
00:57:55,480 --> 00:57:58,250
I mean, an Azalea in this weather?

936
00:57:58,310 --> 00:58:00,820
This is totally a sign from the skies.

937
00:58:01,180 --> 00:58:03,150
We have one applicant coming in the morning, right?

938
00:58:03,220 --> 00:58:06,120
Yes, and they studied abroad.

939
00:58:06,650 --> 00:58:10,790
- The resume is very impressive. - All right.

940
00:58:11,090 --> 00:58:13,190
It is right here, so take a look.

941
00:58:13,260 --> 00:58:14,360
Okay.

942
00:58:14,430 --> 00:58:16,130
- Good luck. - Good luck.

943
00:58:19,300 --> 00:58:23,440
(CEO Baek Mi Young)

944
00:58:26,210 --> 00:58:28,610
(Wedding Dress Order Form)

945
00:59:13,860 --> 00:59:14,860
Hello.

946
00:59:32,510 --> 00:59:34,510
I am the person scheduled for an interview today.

947
00:59:42,780 --> 00:59:47,660
(We would like to thank everyone...)

948
00:59:47,720 --> 00:59:52,330
(for watching OK! Let's Get Divorced.)

949
01:00:11,650 --> 01:00:14,580
(OK! Let's Get Divorced)
